{"reference":"Judges 11","book":"Judges","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Jephthah's vow and his daughter","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter says that Jephthah carried out his vow and repeatedly emphasizes that his daughter remained unmarried. Interpreters therefore disagree about whether the account describes her death or her permanent dedication. The text itself leaves the outcome open enough that readers should recognize the question rather than assume one interpretation settles it.","verse_refs":["Judges 11:29-40"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_011_7bf4df52d4adfdc43cdf3a0d"]}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within Judges","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Jephthah's story belongs to the central deliverance narratives of Judges. The pattern introduced earlier in the book guides these accounts, but the individual episodes do not all follow every stage in the same mechanical sequence. This helps readers attend to the particular shape and tensions of this episode rather than expecting it to repeat a fixed formula.","verse_refs":["Judges 1","Judges 10:1-18","Judges 12:1-15","Judges 13:1-25","Judges 14:1-20","Judges 15:1-20","Judges 16:1-31","Judges 2:1-23","Judges 3:1-31","Judges 3:7-31","Judges 4:1-24","Judges 5:1-31","Judges 6:1-40","Judges 7:1-25","Judges 8:1-35","Judges 9:1-57"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_011_dd6c7160879b9e775430812e"]}]}],"generated_metadata":null}